# Build and commit after each plan

When a plan is fully implemented, the tests pass and the version is bumped (see `version-bump.mdc`), finish without being asked:

1. Export the Windows build:
   `godot --headless --path . --export-release "Windows Desktop" build/Tunelar.exe`
2. Zip it for the LAN updater, using the new version:
   `Compress-Archive -Path build\Tunelar.exe, build\Tunelar.pck -DestinationPath build\Tunelar-X.Y.Z.zip -Force`
3. Commit everything as `Release X.Y.Z`, with a one-paragraph body summarizing the change and pointing to `CHANGELOG.md`. `build/` is gitignored, so only the sources go in.
   - This shell has no git identity, so pass it per commit without changing the git config:
     `git -c user.name="Tom Kocmi" -c user.email="14163064+kocmitom@users.noreply.github.com" commit ...`
4. Do not push unless the user asks.
